# L §5.14 `at e` (round 7): "An `at` that gives a window evaluates the instance once per law-date class, as for a def
# (§4.3): its `when`, legs and attributes are read in each class, and they give one value where all classes agree,
# otherwise HOLE-IMPRECISE unless the line states windows each (L §4.4)."  pay's law date is window(2026-03-01, 2026-03-31); amt
# is 10.00 PLN to 2026-03-14 and 20.00 PLN from 2026-03-15: two classes that disagree, so konto's balance after
# pay's day is a hole (q1); `windows each` splits at the class edge: law date 03-01..03-14 pays 10.00 PLN, plus
# keep's 10.00 (20.00 PLN), 03-15..03-31 pays 20.00 PLN (30.00 PLN) (q2; writer 8: windows latest is gone).  keep's window (2026-01-05 .. 2026-01-20) lies in one class: 10.00 PLN (q3, before pay's day).
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-12-31
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
place konto: accounts PLN lives 2020-01-01..
place world: outside lives 1900-01-01..

input amt: money PLN
input pay_win: date
input keep_win: date
input pay_day: date
input keep_day: date

move pay: transfers
  on pay_day
  at pay_win
  leg cash from world to konto amount amt

move keep: transfers
  on keep_day
  at keep_win
  leg cash from world to konto amount amt

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  pay_win = window(2026-03-01, 2026-03-31)
  keep_win = window(2026-01-05, 2026-01-20)
  pay_day = 2026-04-10
  keep_day = 2026-02-10
  opening[konto] = 0 PLN at 2026-01-01 start

version a1
  cite s
  governs 2026-01-01..2026-03-14
  known 2026-01-01
  amt = 10.00 PLN

version a2
  cite s
  governs 2026-03-15..
  known 2026-01-01
  amt = 20.00 PLN

ask q1: bal(konto, 2026-12-31)
ask q2: bal(konto, 2026-12-31) windows each
ask q3: bal(konto, 2026-03-31)
=== expect
q1: ?"date within window(2026-03-01, 2026-03-31) not precise enough for the law date of pay" (pay)
...
q2 [keep_win = 2026-01-05 .. 2026-01-20, pay_win = 2026-03-01 .. 2026-03-14]: 20.00 PLN
...
q2 [keep_win = 2026-01-05 .. 2026-01-20, pay_win = 2026-03-15 .. 2026-03-31]: 30.00 PLN
...
q3: 10.00 PLN
...
